DESCRIPTION:National Sundae Day falls on November 11 and marks a dish whose
  birthplace two American cities have argued over for more than a century. 
 Two Rivers\, Wisconsin dates the first ice cream sundae to 1881\; Ithaca\,
  New York dates it to 1892 and says it has the newspaper advertisement to 
 prove it. Neither has produced the document that would end the argument.\n
 \nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/national-sundae-day/
